Hi Josep,

Thanks for bringing this up. I agree that we should clean it up. I think
that we should set up an automatic process to flag and then to close stale
pull requests. For instance, we could use a github action [1] for this. I
imagine that we could configure it to mark a pull request as stale after 60
days of inactivity and close it 30 days later if the author does not react.

[1] https://github.com/marketplace/actions/close-stale-issues

Cheers,
David

