Hi Andrew,



> On Jun 13, 2023, at 8:06 AM, Andrew Schofield =
<andrew_schofield_jira@outlook.com> wrote:
>=20
> Hi,
> I would like to start a new discussion thread on KIP-714: Client =
metrics and observability.
>=20
> =
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-714%3A+Client+metric=
s+and+observability
>=20
> I have edited the proposal significantly to reduce the scope. The =
overall mechanism for client metric subscriptions is unchanged, but the
> KIP is now based on the existing client metrics, rather than =
introducing new metrics. The purpose remains helping cluster operators
> investigate performance problems experienced by clients without =
requiring changes to the client application code or configuration.
>=20
> Thanks,
> Andrew

Thanks for the KIP updates. A few questions:

1. The concept of a client instance ID is somewhat similar to the unique =
producer ID that is created for transactional producers. Can we augment =
the name or somehow clarify that this client instance ID is only for use =
by telemetry? The pandora=E2=80=99s box alternative is to make the =
creation, management, etc. of a unique, per-client instance ID a =
first-class construct. I assume that=E2=80=99s something we don=E2=80=99t =
want to bite off in this KIP ;)

2. I=E2=80=99m having trouble understanding where this provision for the =
terminating flag would be useful:

> The Terminating flag may be reused upon the next expiry of =
PushIntervalMs.

In the happy path, the terminating flag is set once at time of =
application shutdown by the close() method of a client. A =
buggy/nefarious client may send multiple push telemetry requests with =
the terminating flag set to skirt throttling. What=E2=80=99s the use =
case where an application would want to send a second request with the =
terminating flag set after PushInteralMs?

3. KIP-848 introduces a new flavor of regex for topic subscriptions. Is =
that what we plan to adopt for the regex used by the subscription match?

4. What=E2=80=99s the benefit of having the broker specify the delta =
temporality if it=E2=80=99s (for now) always delta, besides API protocol =
bumping?

5. What is gained by the existence of the ClientTelemetry interface? Why =
not let interested parties implement ClientTelemetryReceiver directly?

Thanks!=

--Apple-Mail=_E49806B0-8DD9-417D-A5DB-A1CF8F7BEC25--

