Hi Team,

we found new vulnerability introduced in snappy-java-1.1.8.4 library, so we need to get rid of it.

!Screenshot 2023-06-27 at 12.30.51 PM.png|width=321,height=230!

during analysis, we found snappy-java coming via kafka-clients.

As our application is not directly using snappy-java jar.

Can any one please explain what is use of snappy-java in kafka-client or can we exclude that?

Latest kafka-client also having vulnerable snappy-jar, by when kafka-client will release next version which is having non-vulnerable snappy-java jar in it?



--
