[This is a resend with the correct KIP number.]

Hello developers of the Java based consumer,

I submitted https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/13914 to fix a long=20
standing problem that the Kafka consumer on the JVM is not usable from=20
asynchronous runtimes such as Kotlin co-routines and ZIO. However, since=20
it extends the public API I was requested to create a KIP.

So here it is:
KIP-944 Support async runtimes in consumer=20
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/chw0Dw

Any questions, comments, ideas and other additions are welcome!

The KIP should be complete except for the testing section. As far as I=20
am aware there are no tests for the current behavior. Any help in this=20
area would be appreciated.

Kind regards,
 =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 Erik.


--=20
Erik van Oosten
